{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Night at the Planetarium", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Not Just Science Fiction", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future, in spoken interactions or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in a heartbeat ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to do something very quickly, without  thinking about it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: If I were in your shoes, I would cancel in a heartbeat.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about leisure.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "alibi ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an excuse for something bad or a failure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: You're my alibi if I ever need one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "plan ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a set of arrangements for the future ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Man, if I didn't have plans, I would come over and watch it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "temptation", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the \u200bwish to do or have something that you \u200bknow you should not do or have  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't resist the temptation of Star Wars.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "excuse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200breason that you give to \u200bexplain why you did something \u200bwrong ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Ah well, come on! Just give her a better excuse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">May</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Could</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Can't</span> to Speculate about the Present", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "If you want to make guesses about something in the present, you can use special modal verbs like <span class=\"italic\">must, may, might, could</span> and <span class=\"italic\">can't</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of the verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">may/might/could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of the verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">can't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of the verb\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Must</span></span> means that you are almost certain about something. This is the best possible guess. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Can't</span></span> is the opposite of <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">must</span></span> and means that you are almost certain that something is not happening or cannot happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">May, might</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">could</span></span> all have the same meaning and you use them when you are less sure. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">may</span> even discover a whole new passion! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">must</span> cancel on her a lot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am sure you <span class=\"strong\">could</span> reschedule. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It <span class=\"strong\">might</span> be one of the best movies you ever see in your life!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> get angry at you for that. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Zero Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You sometimes need to talk about conditions and possible results or consequences that are real in the present. This is where you need to make a <span class=\"italic\"zero conditional </span>sentence using an if-clause. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a <span class=\"italic\">zero conditional</span> sentence to talk about a general truth or something that happens habitually.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Grammar Structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">if</span> + simple present, simple present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">simple present + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">if</span> + simple present\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Examples:<br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span> I don't get enough sleep, I get sick.<br> I usually go to the beach <span class=\"strong\">if</span> the weather is nice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"italic\">if</span>-clause is the condition clause and can come before or after the result clause. You need to put a comma after the <span class=\"italic\">if</span>-clause if it comes before the result clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Man, <span class=\"strong\">if</span> I <span class=\"strong\">didn't have</span> plans, I <span class=\"strong\">would</span> come over and watch it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> If</span> you felt better, you <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> cancel your plans with her. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">If</span> she <span class=\"strong\">calls</span> you, don't <span class=\"strong\">pick up</span> and tell her later you fell asleep.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use the<span class=\"italic\"> first conditional </span>sentence to talk about a condition that is real and can happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Grammar Structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">if</span> + simple present, will /won't \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">will/won't + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">if</span> + simple present\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If </span> I don't show up, she will never talk to me again. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">second conditional </span>sentence to talk about a condition that is not real or very unlikely to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Grammar Structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">if</span> + simple past, would /wouldn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">if</span> + would /wouldn't, simple past\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If </span> I were in your shoes, I would cancel in a heartbeat.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">Star Wars</span> in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Turn the subtitles on for the first twenty minutes and then off for the next twenty minutes. Continue to alternate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss with a friend whether or not it is likely that we will live in a similar way to those characters in <span class=\"italic\">Star Wars</span> in the future.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch a movie about space.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read the subtitles at times.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express what is likely or unlikely.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to show up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go to a place; to arrive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm meeting a girl, Amanda, tonight. If I don't show up, she will never talk to me again. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about science and leisure time.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  I can express true, untrue and possible events in present.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express what is likely or unlikely.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What is one of your favorite movies and